  "agent": "holmes-mcp",
  "artifact_text": "### Observations\n1. Pod log of `billing-api-665595bbf9-dk4wf` shows recurring `WARN db connection reset by peer, retrying (pool acquire 2.80s)` while pool idle timeout is 900s.\n2. In `ack-system`, `DBProxy/billing-db-proxy` sets `spec.idleClientTimeout: 600`, which is lower than `billing-api`'s `DB_POOL_IDLE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS: 900` configured in deployment `billing-api`.\n3. Pod status shows `billing-api-665595bbf9-dk4wf` is `Running` with 0 restarts and memory at 375Mi under the 512Mi limit.\n\n### Ruled-out Leads\n1. Pod OOMKills or container crashes are ruled out because restart count is 0 and memory is stable at 375Mi below the 512Mi limit.\n2. ALB idle timeout change in deployment `CI-2455` is ruled out because load balancer timeout was increased to 120s, which does not cause RDS connection resets.\n\n### Root Cause\nRDS Proxy (`billing-db-proxy`) closes idle connections after 600s before `billing-api`'s connection pool recycles them at 900s, causing pool exhaustion and failed requests as described in `RB-014`.\n\n### Recommended Action\nThe platform/infrastructure team must raise `spec.idleClientTimeout` on `DBProxy/billing-db-proxy` (or remove it to restore the 1800s default), or the billing team must lower `DB_POOL_IDLE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS` below 600s on deployment `billing-api`.",
